paprika_vdagent_note() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Paprika needs exclusive access to the SPICE virtio port and must start inside
  your graphical session. Complete the persistent setup in:

    /usr/share/doc/paprika-vdagent/setup.md

  The guide covers disabling stock agents, persistent port permissions, and
  automatic X11/Wayland selection and session startup. Enabling the user service
  alone is not sufficient on sessions without a current display environment.

  After completing setup, launch from your desktop or compositor's autostart with:
    paprika-vdagent session-start

  View logs with:
    journalctl --user -u paprika-vdagent.service -b
EOF
}

post_install() {
  paprika_vdagent_note
}

post_upgrade() {
  paprika_vdagent_note
}
